                                "sense_id": "e1b340e9-4ae9-356b-95e3-137025360313",
                                "text": "1798, George Vancouver, A Voyage of Discovery to the North Pacific Ocean, London: G.G. and J. Robinson, Volume I, Chapter II, p. 44, entry for 21 October, 1791,\nI was therefore compelled to relinquish, with great reluctance, the favorite project of further examining the coast of this unknown though interesting country; and, directing our route over an hitherto untraversed part of these seas, we proceeded without further delay towards the pacific ocean."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8db5d28b-2297-44cf-9211-1619072d4ad8",
                                "sense_id": "e1b340e9-4ae9-356b-95e3-137025360313",
                                "text": "In front of us the untraversed plain shone white as a new-laid tablecloth and dazzling even through a pair of smelter’s glasses."
                            }
